\end{align*}
we can expand the right hand side to get
\begin{align*}
4(1989c^2)(a^4-a^2b^2+b^4)-4(a^2)(a^4-a^2b^2+b^4)-4(b^2)(a^4-a^2b^2+b^4)&=7536c^2a^4-7536c^2b^4-4a^6+4a^4b^2-4a^2b^4+4b^6
\end{align*}
We can simplify this equation by factoring out common factors and obtain the following.
\begin{align*}
(4a^4-4a^2b^2+b^4)(1989c^2-a^2-b^2)&=(4a^4-4a^2b^2+b^4)(1989c^2)-4(a^4-a^2b^2+b^4)\\
&=(4a^4-4a^2b^2+b^4)(1989c^2)-4(a^2+b^2-a^2b^2)
\end{align*}
We can factor the last term $a^2+b^2-a^2b^2$ as a difference of squares 
