Using this formula $\frac{\cos(x)-1}{\sin(x)} = \frac{-2\sin^2(x/2)}{2\sin(x/2)\cos(x/2)} = \frac{-\sin(x/2)}{\cos(x/2)}$ placed in the following equation $\frac{1}{\cos(x)-1} = \frac{1}{\frac{-2\sin^2(x/2)}{\sin(\theta)}}$

